## Project Structure (Clean Architecture)

```
├── app/              # Next.js App Router
│   ├── api/          # API routes (health, etc.)
│   ├── (routes)/     # Page routes
│   └── layout.tsx    # Root layout
├── components/       # Reusable UI components
│   ├── ui/           # Primitive components (Button, Input)
│   └── layouts/      # Layout components (Header, Footer)
├── features/         # Feature-based modules (if using)
│   └── auth/         # Example: authentication feature
│       ├── components/
│       ├── hooks/
│       └── types.ts
├── lib/              # Utilities and helpers
│   ├── utils.ts      # Tailwind merge helpers
│   └── cn.ts         # Class name helper
├── public/           # Static assets
├── tailwind.config.ts  # Tailwind configuration
└── compose.yaml      # Deployment config
```

## Tailwind Best Practices

- **Use `cn()` helper** for conditional classes: `cn('base-class', condition && 'active-class')`
- **Avoid arbitrary values** unless absolutely necessary: `w-[123px]` should be `w-32`
- **Group related utilities**: `flex items-center justify-between`
- **Extract repeating patterns** to components or `@apply` in CSS

## Conventions

- TypeScript strict mode enabled
- Environment variables for all config
- Tailwind CSS for all styling (no CSS modules)
- Server Components by default, Client Components only when needed (`'use client'`)
- API routes for backend logic (no server actions in UI components)
